onna blow up the building  and then his alter mr. robot believes  that they need to blow up the building  so there's all this tension and all this  insanity and then you have Darlene  showing up at Angela's place but no one  out of anybody that I just mentioned  actually knows what's going down so that  was very that was very cool and I  definitely give them credit for laying  it out like that because we see what  happens mr. robot finds out that the  documents aren't actually there as a  team him and Elliot get into the room  and saved that building  it feels like a season finale moment of  a cheesy TV show where everybody you  know everything is set  we know it's episode six so it's not the  season finale you're wondering what's  going on  even Elliot's little talk about what  will mr. robot do doesn't have that much  real impact until after what he sees  when he walks down the street in the  same with Darlene and Angela when  they're talking you're like what the  hell you know what I mean like she's not  gonna turn Angela in Angela doesn't  isn't gonna turn so there's all this  cool stuff going on and then Angela and  Darlene both get alerts on their phone  and I didn't even know what that was  like when we were watching it the first  time I was clueless as to what that  indicated I was like is they trying to  make it out like I don't know I had no  idea I was just like what are these what  why did they stop and look at their  phones and when Elliot goes outside this  music says FEM pretty consistent with  the action genre and the end of a high  tense car chase or something like that  you know it goes silent as Elliot sees  the TV and sees what the real deal was  and who's really in charge and that is  whiterose so it was another good episode  it really was like it took me on a  journey  I mean Tyrell is in custody I really  know how that's gonna play out I don't  know if he was supposed to do that or if  I mean we don't know we don't have any  idea what was insi